  "question": {
    "text": "Three identical bars A, B and C are made of different magnetic materials. When kept in a uniform magnetic field, the field lines around them look as follows:\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0061_534b1248daa7.png\"><br><img src=\"assets\\qt0061_312811c435e2.png\"><br><img src=\"assets\\qt0061_d62d83f72603.png\"><br>\nMake the correspondence of these bars with their material being diamagnetic ( $\\mathrm{D})$, ferromagnetic (F) and paramagnetic $(\\mathrm{P})$ :"
